# pyenv
#   For a library or package, you might want to ignore these files since the Python version is
#   something the user should decide. For an application, you might want to commit them.
# .python-version

# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#598, it is recommended to include Pipfile.lock in version control.
#   However, in cases where the lockfile contains platform-specific dependencies, it may be omitted.
#Pipfile.lock

# poetry
#   Similarly, Poetry manages poetry.lock underneath the hood and it is advised to fix the version.
#poetry.lock

# pdm
#   PDM stores project-wide configurations in .pdm.toml:
.pdm.toml
#   and remembers project-local paths in .pdm-python:
.pdm-python
#   PDM also produces a lockfile:
pdm.lock

# PEP 582 spaces
__pypackages__/

